column49:
I find that the braces and termination policy forcibly avoid stuff like:<p><pre><code>   for p = initial; p.next != nil; p = p.next;
       doSomething(p);
</code></pre>
This is a whole class of pain I've had to debug before. Better to be explicit.<p>I'm not really a fan of python indentation as I've had to clean up a couple of messes before.
